        "original_id": "2627d8a2-8d1a-556f-aa31-674d8a55363f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lüliang, Fuxin, Shanxi province, Shaanxi province, Yellow River, Jinzhong, Taiyuan, Linfen, Xinzhou\n- Topics: population, area, administrative geography, census\n\nFacts:\n- Lüliang is a prefecture-level city in western Shanxi province in the People's Republic of China.\n- Lüliang borders Shaanxi province across the Yellow River to the west, Jinzhong and Taiyuan to the east, Linfen to the south, and Xinzhou to the north.\n- Lüliang has a total area of 21,143 km2 and a total population of 3,727,057.\n- At the 2010 census, the Lüliang metro area had a population of 320,142.\n- At the 2010 census, the prefecture of Fuxin had a total population of 1,819,339.\n- At the 2010 census, 669,317 people in Fuxin lived in the built-up area comprising four urban districts collectively known as Fuxin City.",
